    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>.&nbsp; Then the set of all values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, for which&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;for some&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>, is"
